{
  "sn35.73:0.1": "Linked Discourses 35.73 ",
  "sn35.73:0.2": "7. With Migajāla ",
  "sn35.73:0.3": "Six Fields of Contact (3rd) ",
  "sn35.73:1.1": "“Mendicants, anyone who doesn’t truly understand the six fields of contact’s origin, disappearance, gratification, drawback, and escape ",
  "sn35.73:1.2": "has not completed the spiritual journey and is far from this teaching and training.” ",
  "sn35.73:2.1": "When he said this, one of the mendicants said to the Buddha, ",
  "sn35.73:2.2": "“Here, sir, I’m discouraged, really discouraged. ",
  "sn35.73:2.3": "For I don’t truly understand the six fields of contact’s origin, disappearance, gratification, drawback, and escape.” ",
  "sn35.73:3.1": "“What do you think, mendicant? ",
  "sn35.73:3.2": "Is the eye permanent or impermanent?” ",
  "sn35.73:4.1": "“Impermanent, sir.” ",
  "sn35.73:5.1": "“But if it’s impermanent, is it suffering or happiness?” ",
  "sn35.73:6.1": "“Suffering, sir.” ",
  "sn35.73:7.1": "“But if it’s impermanent, suffering, and perishable, is it fit to be regarded thus: ",
  "sn35.73:7.2": "‘This is mine, I am this, this is my self’?” ",
  "sn35.73:8.1": "“No, sir.” ",
  "sn35.73:9.1": "“Is the ear … ",
  "sn35.73:9.2": "nose … ",
  "sn35.73:9.3": "tongue … ",
  "sn35.73:9.4": "body … ",
  "sn35.73:9.5": "mind permanent or impermanent?” ",
  "sn35.73:10.1": "“Impermanent, sir.” ",
  "sn35.73:11.1": "“But if it’s impermanent, is it suffering or happiness?” ",
  "sn35.